  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 17-layer HfO2/SiO2 defect cavity stack on Si substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, SiO2 (defect), SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2. Initialize all thicknesses with ±3% random perturbation around baseline [550, 235, 557, 421, 414, 607, 413, 844, 844, 254, 1705, 284, 2741, 305, 2785, 1056, 1422] nm. Apply optimization bounds: layers 1-10 bounded 280-850 nm, layers 11,13,15,17 bounded 1400-1700 nm, layer 16 bounded 1000-1200 nm, layer 13 bounded 2700-2800 nm. Optimize for maximum mean absorptance in 8000-13000 nm and minimum mean absorptance in 3000-5000 nm at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with 50 iterations maximum. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3000-5000 nm, 8000-13000 nm. soft objectives: high emissivity in 8000-13000 nm; low emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 24.",
